***** for loop *****

for = for each item.

for loop: Use it when you want to repeat something for a list of items or a known number of times.

#!/bin/bash

for i in 1 2 3 4 5
do
    echo "Number is $i"
done

#!/bin/bash -> Run the script using Bash.
for i in 1 2 3 4 5 -> Take each number one by one and store it in i.
do -> Start the commands to repeat.
echo "Number is $i" -> Print the current number.
done -> Finish the loop and move to the next number, if any.

$i means the current value stored in the variable i.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

#!/bin/bash

for service in nginx docker
do
    if systemctl is-active --quiet "$service"; then
        echo "$service is running"
    else
        echo "$service is not running"
    fi
done

This checks the nginx and docker services one by one. Service names can differ by Linux distribution, so verify the names on your server.

